From: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gthreadpool: synchronize idle registration with wakeups

Sample the wakeup serial and register idle workers under a mutex shared
with wakeup producers. Stop unused workers directly without temporarily
changing their configured limit.

Include the public shutdown regression and private scheduling tests from
the reviewed two-commit series:
https://gitlab.gnome.org/tobiasb-ms/glib/-/commit/918fc6f750a127cf3d11db497e703cdc1fc270f6
https://gitlab.gnome.org/tobiasb-ms/glib/-/commit/83548f98ff6407164a7aba13a1a2216950f28e78

Adjust only the Meson registration context for GLib 2.86.5.

While this demonstrates the race, it does not prove that it caused the
original intermittent test failures.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Related: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/work_items/4010
Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
---
